    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0805" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1159</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Erwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1043</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-23">May 23,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received May 28.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my telegram No. 26, May 23, 4
                    p.m., 1940.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d876-f1"/> I received in confidence from the
                    Honduran Foreign Office today through Señor don Fernando Lardizabal, Chief of
                    Protocol, the copy of memorandum <pb facs="0806" n="794" xml:id="pg794"/>
                    submitted to the Honduran Government by the German Minister in Guatemala, which,
                    together with a translation thereof are made enclosures to this despatch.<anchor
                        n="45" xml:id="d876-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>The reply of the Honduran Government has not at this hour been formulated and,
                    therefore, I am not able to state its contents. It will probably be several days
                    before an answer is ready for delivery, as the Foreign Minister<anchor n="46"
                        xml:id="d876-f3"/> must confer with President Carías before anything is
                    done. However, my information is that the response will decline to give any
                    satisfaction to this protest.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Erwin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d876-f1" n="44" xml:id="d876-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated that the Honduran Government received on May 23 similar
                    protest from the German Government, a copy of which Minister Erwin was sending
                    to the Department by air mail (740.00111 A.R./1133).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d876-f2" n="45" xml:id="d876-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d876-f3" n="46" xml:id="d876-f3-content">
                <p>Salvador Aguirre.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
